
# 2026-06-26 17:48:33.048970
+Fix issue #8520: Search endpoint should validate and trim query input.
+
+Changes needed:
+1. Create a new file apps/api/src/validators/search.js with a Zod schema for search query: z.string().trim().max(200).optional().default('')
+2. In apps/api/src/controllers/searchController.js: import the schema, use .parse() on req.query.q, pass the validated query to globalSearch
+3. In apps/api/src/middleware/errorHandler.js: detect ZodError and return HTTP 400 with validation message instead of 500
+
+Keep the code style consistent with the existing codebase (import style, zod usage like in job.js validator).
+
+Criteria from the issue:
+- coerce to a string ✓ (Zod does this by default with .string())
+- trim surrounding whitespace ✓ (.trim())
+- reject overly long input with 400 ✓ (.max(200) + ZodError → 400)
+- keep empty or omitted queries safe ✓ (.optional().default(''))

